* ============================================================
* Vendor-model wrappers — same pins/params as LM317B / LM358B in models.lib,
* so the netlist template only swaps the subcircuit name.
* Vendor files live in ../vendor (see ../vendor/README.md).
* ============================================================
.include ../vendor/onsemi_LM358.mod
.lib ../vendor/LT317A.sub

* ── LM317 (U1): ADI LT317A, LTspice-encrypted ───────────────
* Pins: IN ADJ OUT  (LT317A itself is ADJ OUT IN)
.subckt LM317V in adj out
X1 adj out in LT317A
.ends LM317V

* ── LM358 (U2A / U2B): onsemi LM358 (transistor level, 2018) ─
* Pins: INP INN VCC VEE OUT
* Built-in values measured as a follower on 5 V, 0.2…3.4 V common mode:
* offset -0.42 mV (±0.02), input bias 9.6 nA flowing out of the inputs.
* VOS / IB keep the meaning they have in LM358B (total offset, total bias):
* the wrapper adds only the difference to the model's built-in values.
.subckt LM358V inp inn vcc vee out params: VOS=0 IB=45n
V_os  inp_i inp {VOS+0.42m}
B_ibp vcc inp I = (IB-9.6n)*min(1, max(0, (V(vcc)-V(inp))/0.1))
B_ibn vcc inn I = (IB-9.6n)*min(1, max(0, (V(vcc)-V(inn))/0.1))
X1 inp_i inn vcc vee out LM358
.ends LM358V
